{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-275105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=2,{x}_{2}=-5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $-3.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-275105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) & =(-3)(x-2)(x-(-5)) \\\\  & =-3(x-2)(x+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3(x-2)(x+5) & =-3({x}^{2}+5x-2x-10) \\\\  & =-3({x}^{2}+3x-10) \\\\  & =-3{x}^{2}-9x+30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-3{x}^{2}-9x+30.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-275105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b5249e85559078f26c03fd1d18978af91e5b5d3949241672908e5669e9f03810"} {"question" "q-275105" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-275105" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3x^2-9x+30"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-282069" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,{x}_{2}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $1.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-282069" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-5$ and ${x}_{2}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) & =(1)(x-(-5))(x-4) \\\\  & =(x+5)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)(x-4) & ={x}^{2}-4x+5x-20 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+x-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)={x}^{2}+x-20.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-282069" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b5249e85559078f26c03fd1d18978af91e5b5d3949241672908e5669e9f03810"} {"question" "q-282069" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-282069" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x^2+x-20"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-46582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quadratic polynomial $P(t)$ has roots ${t}_{1}=-5,{t}_{2}=5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $4.$ Find $P(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-46582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${t}_{1}=-5$ and ${t}_{2}=5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t-{t}_{1})(t-{t}_{2}) & =(4)(t-(-5))(t-5) \\\\  & =4(t+5)(t-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(t+5)(t-5) & =4({t}^{2}-25) \\\\  & =4{t}^{2}-100.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(t)=4{t}^{2}-100.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-46582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b5249e85559078f26c03fd1d18978af91e5b5d3949241672908e5669e9f03810"} {"question" "q-46582" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Acad