adratic polynomial has roots ${t}_{1}=4$ and ${t}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t-{t}_{1})(t-{t}_{2}) & =(2)(t-4)(t-3) \\\\  & =2(t-4)(t-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(t-4)(t-3) & =2({t}^{2}-7t+12) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-14t+24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(t)=2{t}^{2}-14t+24.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-46580" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b5249e85559078f26c03fd1d18978af91e5b5d3949241672908e5669e9f03810"} {"question" "q-46580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-46580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{t}^{2}+24t-14"] ["math" "2{t}^{2}-14t+24"] ["math" "2{t}^{2}-7t+12"] ["math" "{t}^{2}+14t+24"] ["math" "{t}^{2}+7t-12"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-46580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{t}^{2}-14t+24"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-107695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quadratic polynomial $P(y)$ has the double root ${y}_{1}={y}_{2}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3.$ Find $P(y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-107695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root ${y}_{1}={y}_{2}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(y-{y}_{1})^{2} & =3{(y-4)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{(y-4)}^{2} & =3({y}^{2}-8y+16) \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}-24y+48.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(y)=3{y}^{2}-24y+48.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-107695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b5249e85559078f26c03fd1d18978af91e5b5d3949241672908e5669e9f03810"} {"question" "q-107695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-107695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{y}^{2}-12y+32"] ["math" "3{y}^{2}-24y+48"] ["math" "3{y}^{2}-3y+96"] ["math" "3{y}^{2}-4y+24"] ["math" "3{y}^{2}-8y+16"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-107695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3{y}^{2}-24y+48"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-104330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has the double root ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=9.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-104330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=9,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})^{2} & =9{(x-(-\\frac{2}{3}))}^{2} \\\\  & =9{(x+\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{(x+\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} & =9({x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}x+\\frac{4}{9}) \\\\  & =9{x}^{2}+12x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=9{x}^{2}+12x+4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-104330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/