options, only $z-(4-3\\text{i})$ is a factor of $3{z}^{2}-24z+75.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-107697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b5249e85559078f26c03fd1d18978af91e5b5d3949241672908e5669e9f03810"} {"question" "q-107697" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-107697" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z-(1-2\\text{i})"] ["math" "z-(2-\\text{i})"] ["math" "z-(3-4\\text{i})"] ["math" "z-(4-3\\text{i})"] ["math" "z-(7-2\\text{i})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-107697" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z-(4-3\\text{i})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-46451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Factor ${x}^{2}-2x+2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-46451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we let $f(x)={x}^{2}-2x+2.$\n\nNext, we solve $f(x)=0$ by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+2 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 1\\cdot x+{1}^{2})-{1}^{2}+2 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-1+2 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & ={\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ x & =1\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since our quadratic equation has roots ${x}_{1}=1+\\text{i}$ and ${x}_{2}=1-\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1,$ the expression ${x}^{2}-2x+2$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x+2 & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-46451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b5249e85559078f26c03fd1d18978af91e5b5d3949241672908e5669e9f03810"} {"question" "q-46451" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-46451" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x-(1+2\\text{i}))(x-(1-2\\text{i}))"] ["math" "(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i}))"] ["math" "(x-(1+\\text{i}))^{2}"] ["math" "(x-(1-\\text{i}))^{2}"] ["math" "(x-(2+\\text{i}))(x-(2-\\text{i}))"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "q-46451" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i}))"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/state.json" "file_sha256" "e99e67c90250f5f2eb3368f47def0dcb4fd2f55f79e091252616f4107a2cf5cd"} {"question" "e-5887" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=2, x_2=5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $3.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/example-5887.json" "file_sha256" "e02a60a54a7fbdab8772cc97175836727b65d2294a6310edcd9e071f87ed1e08"} {"question" "e-5887" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${\\color{black}x_1=2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_2=5},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is ${\\color{black}a=3},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) & =3(x-2)(x-5) \\\\  & =3(x-2)(x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x-2)(x-5) & =3({x}^{2}-7x+10) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-21x+30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = 3x^2-21x+30.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/example-5887.json" "file_sha256" "e02a60a54a7fbdab8772cc97175836727b65d2294a6310edcd9e071f87ed1e08"} {"question" "e-5788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has the double root $x_1=x_2=5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/example-5788.json" "file_sha256" "9b018cc31f4187fccb78a761cb490d9d6a827786eaf500262709a019570d152b"} {"question" "e-5788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root ${\\color{black}x_1=x_2=5},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is ${\\color{black}a=1},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})^{2} & =1\\cdot {(x-5)}^{2} \\\\  & ={(x-5)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x-5)}^{2} & ={x}^{2}-10x+25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = x^2 - 10x+25.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/example-5788.json" "file_sha256" "9b018cc31f4187fccb78a761cb490d9d6a827786eaf500262709a019570d152b"} {"question" "e-5789" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quadratic polynomial $f(z)$ with real coefficients has roots $z_1=3+\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2=3-\\textrm{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $2.$ Find $f(z).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/example-5789.json" "file_sha256" "3d8504405c2e9f311a9a1c53d5dfac71dddf78d61b6d68dad3d00dc94f96a12b"} {"question" "e-5789" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${\\color{black}z_1=3+\\textrm{i}}$ and ${\\color{black}z_2=3-\\textrm{i}},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is ${\\color{black}a=2},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2}) & =2(z-(3+\\text{i}))(z-(3-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(z-(3+\\text{i}))(z-(3-\\text{i})) & =2({z}^{2}-(3+\\text{i})z-(3-\\text{i})z+(3+\\text{i})(3-\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2({z}^{2}-(3+\\text{i}+3-\\text{i})z+({3}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2})) \\\\  & =2({z}^{2}-6z+(9+1)) \\\\  & =2({z}^{2}-6z+10) \\\\  & =2{z}^{2}-12z+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z) = 2z^2-12z+20.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/example-5789.json" "file_sha256" "3d8504405c2e9f311a9a1c53d5dfac71dddf78d61b6d68dad3d00dc94f96a12b"} {"question" "e-5791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Factor $u^2-2u+10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/example-5791.json" "file_sha256" "0e80d2358d2fec10cb0433ee1f2a5536c7fc3a0c150217ee12dbbc390afbe97e"} {"question" "e-5791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we let $f(u) = u^2-2u+10.$\n\nNext, we solve $f(u) = 0$ by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(u) & =0 \\\\ {u}^{2}-2u+10 & =0 \\\\ ({u}^{2}-2u+{1}^{2})-{1}^{2}+10 & =0 \\\\ (u-1)^{2}-1+10 & =0 \\\\ (u-1)^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ (u-1)^{2} & =-9 \\\\ (u-1)^{2} & =9{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ (u-1)^{2} & =(3\\text{i})^{2} \\\\ u-1 & =\\pm 3\\text{i} \\\\ u & =1\\pm 3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since our quadratic equation has roots $u_1=1+ 3\\textrm{i}$ and $u_2=1- 3\\textrm{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1,$ the expression $u^2-2u+10$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-2u+10 & =a(u-{u}_{1})(u-{u}_{2}) \\\\  & =(u-(1+3\\text{i}))(u-(1-3\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978271/example-5791.json" "file_sha256" "0e80d2358d2fec10cb0433ee1f2a5536c7fc3a0c150217ee12dbbc390afbe97e"}] "usage" {"e-5887" [] "e-5788" [] "e-5791" [] "q-46596" [] "q-46580" [] "e-5789" []} "basis" 826 "retractions" [[17592186083631 :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(t)$ has roots $t_{1} = 4, t_{2} = 3$, and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $2$. Find $P(t)$."] [17592186083634 :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $f(z)$ has real coefficients, has roots $z_{1} = 4\\textrm{i}$ and $z_{2} =-4\\textrm{i}$, and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $-1$. Find $f(z)$."] [17592186082961 :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=2, x_2=5$, and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $3$. Find $P(x)$."] [17592186082961 :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_1=2}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_2=5}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the quadratic term is\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}a=3}\n$$\n\nwe can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(x - x_{1})(x - x_{2}) &= 3(x - 2)(x - 5) \\\\\n&= 3(x - 2)(x - 5)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3(x - 2)(x - 5) &= 3(x^{2} - 7x + 10) \\\\\n&= 3x^{2} - 21x + 30\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(x) = 3x^2-21x+30\n$$"] [17592186082954 :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has the double root $x_1=x_2=5$, and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1$. Find $P(x)$."] [17592186082954 :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_1=x_2=5}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the quadratic term is\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}a=1}\n$$\n\nwe can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(x - x_{1})^{2} &= 1 \\cdot (x - 5)^{2} \\\\\n&= (x - 5)^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 5)^{2} &= x^{2} - 10x + 25\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(x) = x^2 - 10x+25\n$$"] [17592186082955 :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $f(z)$ with real coefficients has roots $z_1=3+\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2=3-\\textrm{i}$, and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $2$. Find $f(z)$."] [17592186082955 :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}z_1=3+\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}z_2=3-\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the quadratic term is\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}a=2}\n$$\n\nwe can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(z - z_{1})(z - z_{2}) &= 2(z - (3 + \\textrm{i}))(z - (3 - \\textrm{i}))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(z - (3 + \\textrm{i}))(z - (3 - \\textrm{i})) &= 2(z^{2} - (3 + \\textrm{i})z - (3 - \\textrm{i})z + (3 + \\textrm{i})(3 - \\textrm{i})) \\\\\n&= 2(z^{2} - (3 + \\textrm{i} + 3 - \\textrm{i})z + (3^{2} - \\textrm{i}^{2})) \\\\\n&= 2(z^{2} - 6z + (9 + 1)) \\\\\n&= 2(z^{2} - 6z + 10) \\\\\n&= 2z^{2} - 12z + 20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(z) = 2z^2-12z+20\n$$"] [17592186082956 :question/problem "Factor $u^2-2u+10$."] [17592186082956 :question/worked-solution "First, we let\n\n$$\nf(u) = u^2-2u+10\n$$\n\nNext, we solve\n\n$$\nf(u) = 0\n$$\n\nby completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(u) &= 0 \\\\\nu^{2} - 2u + 10 &= 0 \\\\\n(u^{2} - 2u + 1^{2}) - 1^{2} + 10 &= 0 \\\\\n(u - 1)^{2} - 1 + 10 &= 0 \\\\\n(u - 1)^{2} + 9 &= 0 \\\\\n(u - 1)^{2} &= -9 \\\\\n(u - 1)^{2} &= 9\\textrm{i}^{2} \\\\\n(u - 1)^{2} &= (3\\textrm{i})^{2} \\\\\nu - 1 &= ± 3\\textrm{i} \\\\\nu &= 1 ± 3\\textrm{i}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since our quadratic equation has roots\n\n$$\nu_1=1+ 3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nu_2=1- 3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1$, the expression $u^2-2u+10$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu^{2} - 2u + 10 &= a(u - u_{1})(u - u_{2}) \\\\\n&= (u - (1 + 3\\textrm{i}))(u - (1 - 3\\textrm{i}))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186081153 17592186081154 17592186081155 17592186081156 17592186081157 17592186081171 17592186081172 17592186081173 17592186081174 17592186081175] "immutable_fields" [[17592186081152 :answer-field/correct] [17592186081152 :answer-field/id] [17592186081152 :answer-field/key] [17592186081152 :answer-field/type] [17592186081170 :answer-field/correct] [17592186081170 :answer-field/id] [17592186081170 :answer-field/key] [17592186081170 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
